     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The only difference between two models are the position of &quot;attacking&quot; in #regression equation. </div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>That is unexpected.  Could you post some data to reproduce the problem?  You could also compare the parameter tables </div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">PT6 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lavaanify</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">auto</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>PT7 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lavaanify</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">auto</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><div><br></div></div><div>By the way, this is problematic:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#residual correlations</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      value     </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">value<br>      rating    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rating</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div>You are not specifying correlations, you are fixing residual variances to 1.  That is too restrictive because you are also fixing the first factor loading of each of those constructs to 1 (<a href=\"http://std.lv\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427313470000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1yWI6hshylCho1qSeO7txO\">std.lv</a> = FALSE implies that, check your parameter table or<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> summary() </font>output).  Since value is regressed on rating, you cannot additionally estimate a residual covariance/correlation anyway, and fixing it to a nonzero value would just attenuate the estimate of the regression slope<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> value~rating</font>.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427313470000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3e4_eXyMkOWQkCACk6GDJD\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
